; host-exec-starved-probe.fk — run me inside a fork-starved fkwu; my final
; value is one token carrying two readings: the tens digit is (nothing? r) for
; a host-exec whose sh could not launch, the ones digit is 1 when (str_len r)
; still answers 0 — the graceful floor length-guarded callers stand on.
; Unstarved this cell answers 0: date speaks bytes, so both digits fall.
;
; Driven by form/form-stdlib/tests/host-exec-launch-honesty-band.fk through
;   ulimit -u 1; exec ./fkwu observe/host-exec-starved-probe.fk
; ulimit is a shell builtin and exec replaces without forking, so the
; starvation reaches host-exec's popen and only it.
; witnessed: 2026-08-27 -> 11 starved, 0 unstarved
(do (let r (host-exec "date +%s%N" ""))
    (add (mul 10 (nothing? r)) (if (eq (str_len r) 0) 1 0)))
